# PoLaRiS: Point-spread Function Reconstruction of Stellar Sources

PoLaRiS is an automated pipeline for point spread function (PSF) modeling
and reconstruction from multi-band astronomical imaging data. It is
currently optimized for the Kilo-Degree Survey and the DESI Legacy Imaging
Surveys.

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Radit-Raian/PoLaRiS.git
cd PoLaRiS
pip install -e .
```

SExtractor must also be built and installed separately:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/astromatic/sextractor
cd sextractor
sh autogen.sh
./configure
make -j
sudo make install
sex   # confirm it's on PATH
```

## Configuration

All paths, per-patch parameters (flux-radius / magnitude windows, cutout
sizes, normalization annuli, masking thresholds) and plotting constants
live in `polaris/config.py`. Edit that file — or set the
`POLARIS_FITS_DIR`, `POLARIS_GAIA_DIR`, and `POLARIS_SEX_BIN` environment
variables — before running the pipeline on a new dataset.

## Usage

See `examples/quickstart.ipynb` for a runnable walkthrough — including a self-contained demo
of the stacking + rotation-randomization logic on synthetic data that needs no external
dependencies or real survey tiles.

Run the full pipeline:

```bash
python run_pipeline.py
```

Resume from a specific step (useful once earlier steps have already
produced their outputs):

```bash
python run_pipeline.py --from stacking
```

Or run any step on its own:

```bash
python -m polaris.stacking
python -m polaris.radial_profile
```

## Pipeline steps

| Module | Step |
|---|---|
| `preprocessing.py` | Inspect raw FITS tiles |
| `run_sextractor.py` | Configure and run SExtractor per tile |
| `background.py` | Visualize background subtraction |
| `point_sources.py` | Identify point sources, adaptive CLASS_STAR threshold |
| `gaia_validation.py` | Cross-match against Gaia, build master catalog |
| `star_selection.py` | Define and visualize Core/Intermediate/Outer_1/Outer_2 patches |
| `cutouts.py` | Extract per-star cutouts |
| `masking.py` | Mask contaminating neighboring objects |
| `stacking.py` | Normalize, reject, randomly rotate, and stack |
| `radial_profile.py` | Stitch per-patch profiles into one continuous PSF radial profile |

